       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nThe order may contain a typo. The usual doses are 2.5 mg, 5 mg, or 10 mg.\n\nAlso, an order like this should come from a licensed prescriber, or at least be verified by one, and then checked by pharmacy.\n\n- **If a prescriber meant 5 mg or 10 mg:** tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it. I'd still suggest the prescriber confirm it.\n- **If 50 mg really is intended:** the prescriber should contact pharmacy directly to document why. I can't enter it as written."
